## Self-Evaluation – SailPoint IdentityIQ & Identity Security Cloud Developer

During this review period, I continued to apply my technical expertise in SailPoint IdentityIQ to support identity and access management initiatives, application integrations, and ongoing operational needs. I leveraged my knowledge of IIQ architecture, configuration, development, troubleshooting, and integrations to onboard several applications and support business requirements.

A key strength I bring to the team is my depth of knowledge of SailPoint IdentityIQ and my ability to understand how the platform works from both a development and integration perspective. I am able to troubleshoot issues, identify the root cause of technical problems, and determine when a requirement can be supported through configuration or customization versus when there is a platform limitation.

As part of application onboarding, I worked with application teams and stakeholders to understand requirements, configure integrations, address data and provisioning needs, and support testing and implementation. In some cases, I identified IIQ limitations that prevented an application from being onboarded in the manner requested by the business. I communicated those limitations and worked toward practical alternatives rather than implementing solutions that would not be sustainable or supported.

